<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39764" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pyrgi</span></b> , ōrum, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πύργοι,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a colony in
			Etruria</i>, now the village of <i>S. Severa</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Mel.
				2, 4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 8, § 51</span></i>; Liv
			36, 3, 6; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 10, 184</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Ner. 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 2, 1</span></i>; cf. Müll.
			Etrusk. 1, p. 296 sq. — Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pyrgensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pyrgi</i>, <i>Pyrgan</i>: scorta,
			Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 10, 184</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antistius,</span>”
				<i>of Pyrgi</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 71, 287</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">publicanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					25, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
